# pokeemerald-expansion

This is a GBA ROM hack base built on pret's pokeemerald decompilation. It adds features from Generations 4–9, an expanded battle engine, and extensive configurability.

## Hardware & Toolchain
- Target: Game Boy Advance (ARM7TDMI CPU, ARMv4T)
- Compiler: `arm-none-eabi-gcc`, standard `gnu17`, Thumb mode (`-mthumb -mthumb-interwork`)
- Build system: GNU Make (`Makefile` at repo root)
- ROM output: `pokeemerald.gba` (32MB max)

## Primary Customization Surface
All feature toggles live in `include/config/`:
- `battle.h` — battle mechanics, damage formula, critical hits, etc.
- `pokemon.h` — species limits, egg groups, level caps
- `ai.h` — AI difficulty and behavior flags
- `overworld.h` — overworld engine settings
- `item.h`, `save.h`, `general.h`, `debug.h`, `caps.h`

Prefer editing these config headers over modifying engine source when possible.

## Key Constraints
- No heap allocation (`malloc`) in performance-critical or battle code — use static/stack allocation
- No standard I/O (`printf`, `scanf`) — GBA has no OS
- No threads — single-threaded with a task/callback system
- IWRAM (32KB fast RAM) is precious; annotate time-critical functions with `IWRAM_CODE`

## Documentation
All how-to guides are in `docs/tutorials/`. Read the relevant tutorial before adding new Pokémon, moves, trainers, or battle script commands.
